<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Dawn - A journey to the beginning of the solar system</title>
<script type="text/javascript" id="MathJax-script" async
  src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js">
</script>
<style>
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    background: #000;
    color: #fff;
    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    width: 2508px;
    max-width: 100%;
  }
  .page {
    position: relative;
    padding: 20px 40px 40px 40px;
  }
  .title-block {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    padding-top: 10px;
  }
  .title-block h1 {
    font-size: 64px;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #6fd6f0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .title-block h2 {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #6fd6f0;
    margin: 5px 0 0 0;
  }
  .main-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 900px 1fr;
    gap: 20px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 60px;
  }
  .section h3 {
    color: #6fd6f0;
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin: 0 0 10px 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .flag {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 34px;
    height: 22px;
    vertical-align: middle;
    border: 1px solid #444;
  }
  .flag.de {
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, #000 33%, #d00 33%, #d00 66%, #ffce00 66%);
  }
  .flag.us {
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(to bottom, #b22234 0 8%, #fff 8% 16%);
  }
  .flag.it {
    background: linear-gradient(to right, #008C45 33%, #F4F5F0 33% 66%, #CD212A 66%);
  }
  .section p {
    font-size: 16px;
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: bold;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin: 0 0 12px 0;
  }
  .section-body {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 15px;
  }
  .section-body.reverse {
    flex-direction: row-reverse;
    text-align: right;
  }
  .section-body.reverse p {
    text-align: right;
  }
  .placeholder {
    background: #1a1a1a;
    border: 1px dashed #555;
    color: #999;
    font-size: 12px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    text-align: center;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }
  .instrument-img {
    width: 220px;
    height: 220px;
  }
  .portrait {
    width: 110px;
    height: 110px;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }
  .caption {
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 6px;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }
  .person-block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .stack {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
  }
  .flex-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 15px;
  }
  .center-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    padding-top: 30px;
  }
  .center-img {
    width: 850px;
    height: 720px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .center-caption {
    font-size: 20px;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-top: 20px;
    max-width: 800px;
  }
  .url-link {
    color: #6fd6f0;
    font-size: 34px;
    font-weight: bold;
    font-style: italic;
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 30px;
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
  }
  .gamma-section {
    display: flex;
    gap: 15px;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }
  .gamma-img {
    width: 260px;
    height: 260px;
  }
  .gamma-text-col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">

  <div class="title-block">
    <h1>Dawn</h1>
    <h2>A journey to the beginning of the solar system</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="main-grid">

    <!-- LEFT COLUMN -->
    <div class="col">
      <div class="section">
        <h3><span class="flag de"></span>Framing Cameras</h3>
        <p>By imaging the surfaces of Vesta and Ceres, the framing cameras will enable scientists to map the topography, albedo and color, and to determine their shapes, volumes, and spin rates.</p>
        <div class="flex-row">
          <div class="person-block">
            <div class="placeholder portrait" style="width:110px;height:110px;">[Photo]</div>
            <div class="caption">Holger Sierks<br>Framing Camera Lead, MPS</div>
          </div>
          <div class="placeholder instrument-img" style="width:220px;height:260px;">[Instrument: Framing Camera hardware]</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h3><span class="flag us"></span>Gamma Ray Neutron Detector</h3>
        <div class="gamma-section">
          <div class="placeholder gamma-img" style="width:250px;height:280px;">[Instrument: GRaND detector, 3D rendering]</div>
          <div class="gamma-text-col">
            <p>GRaND measures elemental abundances on the surfaces of Vesta and Ceres, offering insight into their respective formation and evolution</p>
            <div class="person-block">
              <div class="placeholder portrait" style="width:100px;height:100px;">[Photo]</div>
              <div class="caption">Tom Prettyman<br>GRaND Team Lead, PSI</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- CENTER COLUMN -->
    <div class="center-col">
      <div class="placeholder center-img">[Image: Dawn spacecraft orbiting Vesta/Ceres, red orbit trajectory, yellow signal beam to surface]</div>
      <div class="center-caption">
        In its journey to the main asteroid belt to orbit two diverse protoplanets, Vesta and Ceres, Dawn is carrying a suite of sophisticated scientific instruments to collect data that will inform us about the early formation of our solar system.
      </div>
      <a class="url-link" href="http://dawn.jpl.nasa.gov">http://dawn.jpl.nasa.gov</a>
    </div>

    <!-- RIGHT COLUMN -->
    <div class="col">
      <div class="section">
        <h3 style="justify-content:flex-start;"><span class="flag us"></span>Gravity Science</h3>
        <div class="section-body">
          <p>Gravity science: the spacecraft transmits a radio signal to Earth through its high gain antenna that changes in frequency as the spacecraft's speed changes when flying over areas of different densities. The collective set of information on the mass variations or concentrations is called the gravitational field of the body/planet.</p>
          <div class="placeholder instrument-img" style="width:260px;height:200px;flex-shrink:0;">[Instrument: High gain antenna &amp; solar panel]</div>
        </div>
        <div class="person-block" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="placeholder portrait" style="width:100px;height:100px;">[Photo]</div>
          <div class="caption">Sami Asmar<br>Gravity Science Lead, JPL</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section">
        <h3><span class="flag it"></span>Visible &amp; Infrared Spectrometer</h3>
        <div class="section-body">
          <div class="placeholder instrument-img" style="width:260px;height:220px;flex-shrink:0;">[Instrument: VIR spectrometer hardware]</div>
          <p>VIR measures reflected sunlight and emitted thermal radiation from the surfaces of the targets. Scientists extract and then map mineralogical signatures and thermal properties. These properties hold clues to the history and formation mechanisms of Vesta and Ceres.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="person-block" style="margin-top:10px; align-items:flex-end;">
          <div class="placeholder portrait" style="width:100px;height:100px;">[Photo]</div>
          <div class="caption">Angioletta Coradini,<br>VIR Team Leader, INAF</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
